/* English translation of the text blocks of the page, keyed by block index (DOM order of leaf blocks h1,h2,h3,p,li,td,th,figcaption in main). Blocks without an entry (already English, dates, etc.) are left unchanged. */
window.EIS_EN={"0": "Introductory Text to the Canonical Memorandum of the Drafting Committee of Theologians, Jurists and Scholars of the Holy Church of All Saints, Patras, for the Information of Orthodox Everywhere", "1": "<u>The Church of the G.O.C. of Greece has broken away from the Catholic Orthodox Church,</u> now teaching, even synodically, doctrines alien to the ecclesiastical Tradition and to the teaching of the Fathers, contrary to that which has been believed always, everywhere and by all, the criterion that constitutes the dogma of Catholicity and of the Unity of the Confession of the Faith and of Orthodoxy", "2": "<em>“What the Bishop of Attica and the Bishop of Thessaloniki do — <strong>the official joint celebrations, the exchanges of festal palm branches, blessed on both sides, with Ecumenist New Calendarists and by bishops of the church of the G.O.C. of Greece at the great feasts over a series of years, the joint prayers with the Ecumenists, the very frequent administration of Holy Communion by the bishops and priests of the church of the G.O.C. of Greece to the New Calendarists, the continual fraternizing and mingling with the New Calendarists, the granting of the chanter’s stand to New Calendarist chanters, the permissions for New Calendarist priests to give talks inside Orthodox Churches — they do these things because the</strong> <strong>heresy of Cyprianism has come to dominate the Church of the G.O.C. of Greece! Every Orthodox reaches the same conclusion when he sees the Indonesian priests and their bishop Mr. Daniel Biantoro continually praying together with the hodgepodge of the Protestants for almost three years, and indeed while vested! This long-standing tolerance is a betrayal of the Faith and echoes the Cyprianite Ecumenist and heretical ideology.”</strong></em>", "3": "<em><strong>“If, then, we commemorate them, or attend a church where those from whom we have walled ourselves off are commemorated, on the one hand our walling-off is undermined, and on the other the anathemas against Ecumenism and Cyprianism seize us!</strong> Matters, according to <strong>Saint Theodore the Studite,</strong> we do not view locally and in isolation, we who “seem to be something,” but with a view to the future, and also honoring our Fathers and our Holy Tradition! Otherwise, in our <strong>Synodikon of Orthodoxy,</strong> which only we read in full on the Sunday of Orthodoxy, we would be continually anathematizing ourselves and the future generations would anathematize us too! <strong>Where, then, those of the Church of the G.O.C. of Greece are commemorated, we do not attend, because we share in the defilement, and the anathema of all the great Genuine Orthodox Synods throughout the world, which anathematized the false doctrines of the church of the G.O.C. of Greece, seizes us in earnest! It is a matter of respect for the Orthodoxy of our Fathers and concerns our salvation! It is not simply some administrative matter or a matter of violations of some administrative Canons! We who “seem to be something” give the mark and lead our simpler brethren!”</strong></em>", "4": "<em><strong>“Many important brethren, bishops and priests in Greece and abroad have rejected the church of the G.O.C. of Greece as Sergianist, Uniate and as tainted by the Cyprianite heretical ideology!</strong> All those who rejected them were members of the Church of the G.O.C. of Greece! We were late... Unfortunately<strong>! And Archbishop Kallinikos signed and justified the violations of the dogmatic Canons, and what was wrongly done received synodal authority through their anti-patristic decision!</strong> They proclaimed that the things mentioned and many others, without number, are supposedly <strong>“social courtesies” and “social protocol”!!! This is the heresy of Relativism, the most significant manifestation of Ecumenism and Cyprianism (Relativism)! Cyprianism was condemned by all, the Romanians, the Russians and all the other Synods in Greece, as Ecumenism and Relativism!</strong></em>", "5": "<em><strong>The condemnatory decisions of the Romanians and the Russians, as well as the rejections of the church of the G.O.C. of Greece</strong> by important figures of Orthodoxy in Greece and on Mount Athos, we publish below! <strong>We are not in the Old Calendar only for thirteen days or out of some romanticism, but we struggle with the blood of our heart for the sacred and holy things of our Orthodoxy!”</strong></em>", "6": "<strong>With Whom We Commune: Saint Theodore the Studite</strong><a class=\"footnote-ref\" href=\"#fn1\" id=\"fnref1\" role=\"doc-noteref\"><sup>1</sup></a>, referring ad hoc to this question, determines with absolute patristic documentation, <strong>“according to all the Saints,”</strong> the marks of the <strong>“unimpeachable”</strong> and <strong>“uncondemned”</strong> Cleric with whom the struggling Orthodox ought, in a time of heretical confusion, to have communion,", "7": "<strong>a.</strong> because, according to the <strong>Saint,</strong> heresy is not the only obstacle to communion; there are other obstacles too: those of a canonical nature, as also those <em><strong>“suspected and heard of as faulty in the course of life”</strong></em>;", "8": "<strong>b.</strong> because the canonical obstacles and the <em><strong>“manifestly”</strong> <strong>“faulty in the course of life,”</strong> <strong>“even if secondary,”</strong></em> in relation to heresy, are “<em><strong>yet not lesser for those who consider piously,”</strong></em> inasmuch as <em><strong>“the one is struck by the other”</strong></em>;", "9": "<strong>c.</strong> because the so timely patristic exhortation remains in force also today: <em>“<strong>Inquire, be diligent; for uninvestigated communion is not without danger; for the danger is over great matters”</strong></em> (of Saint Chrysostom); <em>“</em>(let us) <em><strong>therefore seek out and be diligent about from whom we ought to commune.”</strong></em>", "10": "Cyprianism, unfortunately, has come to dominate within the church of the G.O.C. of Greece and everywhere, in the holy Monasteries, in the Parishes and in the flock of the church of the G.O.C., and is now the belief of the majority of the adherents of that faction, of Cyprianism.", "11": "<strong>Those of the Church of the G.O.C. of Greece commune all the New Calendarists, both their so-called <em>“canonical”</em> bishops and almost all their priests,</strong> (there are also some exceptions). This alone suffices <strong>for the breaking of our communion with them and for their rejection as Orthodox.</strong>", "12": "Synodically and officially, however, the bishops of the church of the G.O.C. of Greece ratified the Ecumenist proclamations and the unacceptable actions of the Bishop of Attica, Mr. Maniotis, and of his cousin, the Bishop of Thessaloniki, Mr. Markopoulos.", "13": "The most important thing to be taken particularly into account is the <strong>Great Synodal anathema of the Romanian bishops against the church of the G.O.C. of Greece under Archbishop Kallinikos Sarantopoulos. This was the most important and decisive event, which led us to the final breaking of our communion with the church of the G.O.C. of Greece under Archbishop Kallinikos.</strong>", "14": "This fact must be evaluated appropriately by all Genuine Orthodox, and they must take final and irrevocable decisions for the definitive breaking of their communion with the faction now called the church of the G.O.C. of Greece.", "15": "<strong>The Romanian Synod is the largest Orthodox synod in the world! The present Romanian Synod under Metropolitan Eulogios is most canonical and was in full communion with the church of the G.O.C. of Greece of Archbishop Kallinikos when, under the late-lamented Metropolitan Demosthenes, they broke communion with Archbishop Kallinikos and those under him. Subsequently the bishops of the Romanian Church under the leadership of Metropolitan Eulogios clearly anathematized, by their decision, the heretical beliefs of the church of the G.O.C. of Greece!</strong>", "16": "<strong>a. It is not only the Romanian Synod,</strong> however, that rejected and anathematized the synod of the church of the G.O.C. of Greece under Archbishop Kallinikos Sarantopoulos, but <strong><u>there are also many other condemnations,</u></strong> such as", "17": "<strong>b.</strong> the condemnation by the <strong>Genuine Orthodox Russian Synod of Archbishop Tikhon,</strong> which <strong>was synodically the first to reject, condemn and anathematize them,</strong>", "18": "<strong>c. but also the largest Genuine Orthodox <u>Russian Synod</u> in the world under Metropolitan Theodore of Suzdal</strong>", "19": "<strong>d. and the Russian Archbishop Stephen with his Synod!</strong>", "20": "All these <u>condemned and anathematized Cyprianism and the union of the Cyprianites with Archbishop Kallinikos and consequently condemned the Cyprianite heretical ideology, which prevails today in the whole sphere of the faction of the church of the G.O.C. of Greece under Archbishop Kallinikos!</u> The most basic proof of the prevailing heresy of Cyprianism in the church of the G.O.C. of Greece is that almost all the priests and the hierarchs of this synod commune all the New Calendarist faithful. And for this reason they are anathematized by the Romanian Synod of Metropolitan Eulogios and all the genuine Orthodox bishops throughout the world have condemned them as Ecumenists.", "21": "<strong>Thus their Synodal condemnation by many Synods of Genuine Orthodox throughout the world (of Romanians and Russians) came first, and then we, having exhausted every economy, rejected them finally and irrevocably.</strong> The breaking of our communion with the synod of the church of the G.O.C. of Greece is <strong>final and irrevocable. <u>We did not become a super-synod,</u></strong> but simply followed the synods and the multitude of bishops and of important Orthodox brethren who rejected and anathematized them!", "22": "We followed the stance of <strong>the largest Canonical Synod in the world,</strong> (which also has the most faithful), <strong>the Romanian</strong> and the stance of many other Orthodox Synods, such as <strong>that of Metropolitan Theodore of Suzdal</strong>, <strong>of Archbishop Tikhon, of Archbishop Stephen</strong> and <strong>of many other Greek and Russian Archbishops and bishops</strong>, <strong>who rejected and condemned them,</strong> breaking communion with them. Important personalities, too, who belonged to the sphere of the church of the G.O.C. of Greece rejected them as well, as we will see below!", "23": "It is shown today, (in the last decade), that <strong>those of the church of the G.O.C. of Greece under Archbishop Kallinikos are an appendage of the New Calendarists.</strong>", "24": "Unfortunately, this is confirmed from many sides:", "25": "They never believed what we agreed in 2014.", "26": "They are like chameleons!", "27": "They change color, depending on the environment; in one place they appear with the mask of genuine Orthodox and in another with Cyprianite ideology…", "28": "Let us look again at what the patriarchs of the East with their Synods (1848) proclaim synodically about <strong>who it is that judges both patriarchs and bishops and synods. Those of the church of the G.O.C. of Greece tremble at the proclamation of the Patriarchs of the Pan-Orthodox Synod of 1848: The Guardian and defender of Orthodoxy is this very people of God, the Royal priesthood, the Holy nation!</strong>", "29": "We too, therefore, applied the <em><strong>“A man that is an heretick after the first and second admonition reject; knowing that he that is such is subverted, and sinneth, being condemned of himself</strong>”</em> (Titus 3:10–11). <strong>The Great Apostle Paul</strong> instructs his disciple Titus to admonish the heretical man, but if he persists in his error, <strong>like the Bishop of Attica, Mr. Maniotis, after the first and the second admonition, every genuine Orthodox should avoid further association with him and with those who commune with him.</strong> The word <strong>“reject” (<i>paraitou</i>)</strong> means <strong>“avoid,” “keep away,” “do not accept.”</strong> The word <strong>“self-condemned”</strong> indicates that this man, by consciously persisting in his error, like the Bishop of Attica, Mr. Maniotis, and his accomplice, his cousin, the Bishop of Thessaloniki, Mr. Markopoulos, <strong>makes himself solely responsible for his condemnation, <u>he is self-condemned.</u> This we too ascertained, on the basis of the Holy tradition of our Church and the decisions of the Ecumenical and Pan-Orthodox Synods, and also the Unification Text of 2014, and we broke communion with such persons <u>and with those in communion with them.</u></strong>", "30": "Russian Old Calendarist Genuine Orthodox Synods that condemned the ecclesiological deviations of the Synod of Archbishop Kallinikos Sarantopoulos concerning the heresy of Cyprianism, which is preached in practice by his Synod, his bishops and the priests of his Synod", "31": "From thorough research it emerges that the Russian Genuine Orthodox Church (<strong>Russian True Orthodox Church – RTOC</strong>) made an express synodal condemnation of the union of the Synod of Archbishop Kallinikos Sarantopoulos with the Synod of the Resisters (Cyprianites) in 2014.", "32": "This condemnation has particular theological and canonical significance, because it <strong>concerns</strong> not simply administrative differences, but <strong>the question of the ecclesiology of Cyprianism, of the acceptance of previously condemned teachings and of union without prior repentance.</strong>", "33": "1. The Russian Genuine Orthodox Church (RTOC)", "34": "<strong>Synodal decision</strong> published on 12 December 2014.", "35": "<strong>The Synod of Bishops of the RTOC examined the union of the Church of the G.O.C. of Greece under Archbishop Kallinikos with the Cyprianites and</strong> in its decision:", "36": "It invokes the Anathema of 1983 against Ecumenism, which was issued by <strong>the Russian Church Outside of Russia (ROCOR).</strong>", "37": "<strong>It characterizes the ecclesiology of the Synod of the Resisters as covert Ecumenism.</strong>", "38": "<strong>It points out that no repentance of the Cyprianites is observed, nor any renunciation of their former ecclesiological positions.</strong>", "39": "<strong><u>It recognizes the significance of the earlier condemnatory decisions of the Greek Synod under the ever-memorable Archbishop Mr. Chrysostomos against the Cyprianites.</u></strong>", "40": "<strong>It regards the union as a grave ecclesiological error and as union with schismatics and crypto-Ecumenists.</strong>", "41": "<strong>The decision concludes with the assessment that the union constitutes a fall of the Greek Synod into communion with schismatics and crypto-Ecumenists.</strong> Source: <a href=\"https://nftu.net/rtoc-synod-officially-condemns-goc-k-union/?utm_source=chatgpt.com\"><u>RTOC Synod Officially Condemns GOC-K Union (12.12.2014)</u></a>", "42": "2. A more recent official statement of the same Russian Synod - 26 September 2015", "43": "<strong>The Chancellery of the RTOC, through Protopresbyter Victor Melehov,</strong> returned to the matter. The statement expressly mentions the Synod under the omophorion of Archbishop Kallinikos, and <strong>points out the serious canonical and ecclesiological errors committed by the union of March 2014.</strong> The Russian side considers that <strong>the Greek Hierarchy departed from its previous confession, having united with the Synod of the Resisters without requiring a renunciation of its ecclesiological teachings.</strong> This is an official confirmation of the earlier condemnatory position. Source: <a href=\"https://nftu.net/rtoc-chancellory-issues-additional-statement-concerning-gock-sir-union/?utm_source=chatgpt.com\"><u>RTOC Chancellery - Statement 26.09.2015</u></a>", "44": "3. The Russian Orthodox Autonomous Church of Metropolitan Theodore of Suzdal (ROAC)", "45": "<strong>Synodal condemnation of 17 February 2007</strong> - published Minutes of the Synod in 2008.", "46": "<strong>The Russian Orthodox Autonomous Church</strong> (<strong>Russian Orthodox Autonomous Church – (ROAC) of Theodore, Metropolitan of Suzdal</strong> is a different ecclesiastical jurisdiction from the <strong>RTOC. Its Synod condemned the ecclesiology of Metropolitan Cyprian of Oropos and Fyli, characterizing it as a teaching that covertly introduces the heresy of Ecumenism.</strong> The synodal decision proclaims that <strong>those who accept the specific teaching fall under the Anathema of ROCOR of 1983. sinod.ruschurchabroad.org+1</strong> Primary evidence: <a href=\"https://roacusa.org/Documents/SOBOR_2008_Protocols.html?utm_source=chatgpt.com\"><u>Minutes of the Synod of ROAC of 2008</u></a> This decision is of very great significance for the union of 2014.", "47": "4. The Russian Church Outside of Russia (ROCOR) and the Anathema of 1983", "48": "<strong>The Synod of ROCOR under Saint Philaret issued in 1983 the well-known Anathema against Ecumenism.</strong> This Anathema is a basic dogmatic piece of evidence, to which the later Russian condemnatory decisions on Cyprianism refer, and <strong>it condemns also the Synod of Archbishop Kallinikos and the bishops and priests who preach in an Ecumenist manner, by word and deed, -(the openings toward the Ecumenists and the New Calendarists)-, the heresy of Cyprianism.</strong>", "49": "5. A later, second synodal condemnation of Cyprianism by the RTOC", "50": "In a separate synodal text of the RTOC, published in 2017, with the title:", "52": "<strong>the ecclesiological heresy of Cyprianism is condemned and the heresy of Sergianism is anathematized.</strong> The Synod reaffirms that <strong>Cyprianism constitutes an ecclesiological heresy, which falls under the Anathema of 1983.</strong> Source: <a href=\"https://trueorthodox.eu/determination-of-the-sobor-of-bishops-of-rtoc-concerning-dogmatic-questions-regarding-the-sacraments-of-world-ecumenical-orthodoxy-the-ecclesiological-heresy-of-cyprianism-and-the-anathematizing/?utm_source=chatgpt.com\"><u>Synodal text of the RTOC on Cyprianism</u></a>", "53": "Summary table", "54": "<strong>Russian Synod</strong>", "55": "<strong>Date</strong>", "56": "<strong>Content</strong>", "59": "Anathema against Ecumenism in general", "62": "<strong>Condemnation of the ecclesiology of Cyprian</strong>", "65": "<strong>Express condemnation of the union of the Synod of Kallinikos with the Cyprianites</strong>", "68": "<strong>Official confirmation of the errors imputed</strong>", "70": "2017 (publication)", "71": "<strong>Reaffirmation of the condemnation of Cyprianism</strong>", "72": "Canonical conclusion", "73": "From the above it emerges that two distinct Russian Old Calendarist ecclesiastical jurisdictions, <strong>ROAC</strong> and <strong>RTOC, have synodically condemned the ecclesiology of Cyprianism, apart from the condemnation by the Great Romanian Synod.</strong>", "74": "Of these, the <strong>RTOC has expressly condemned, as we saw, also the union of the Synod of Kallinikos with the Cyprianites.</strong> Of particular significance is also the official study of Protopresbyter <strong>Victor Melehov,</strong> which is published on the website of the <strong>RTOC</strong> and examines in detail the union of 2014. <a href=\"https://www.ripc.info/en/library/doc/protopresb-victor-melehov-a-commentary-on-the-union-between-the-gtoc-and-the-greek-synod-in-resist/?utm_source=chatgpt.com\"><u>Victor Melehov - Critique of the union of G.O.C. and Cyprianites</u></a> <strong>Victor Melehov</strong> belongs to the Russian Genuine Orthodox Church (<strong>RTOC</strong> – RIPC), whose <strong>Primate is Archbishop Tikhon of Omsk and Siberia</strong> (Pasechnik). Indeed, there is a significant recent development: <strong>Victor Melehov</strong> served as Protopresbyter and Secretary of the Holy Synod of Archbishop Tikhon. <strong>On 14 September 2025 he was ordained Bishop of Boston and America, by hierarchs of the RTOC.</strong> He continues to be included in the official composition of the Synod of Archbishop Tikhon. Therefore, <strong>Victor Melehov</strong> is not simply an independent theologian who criticized the Synod of Kallinikos Sarantopoulos. He belongs to the same Russian ecclesiastical jurisdiction that issued the condemnatory decision on the union of 2014 with the Cyprianites. Of particular significance is that a theological text of his of 2018 was published with the blessing of the Synod of the RTOC.", "75": "The official stance of the Great Synod of Metropolitan Theodore (successor of Metropolitan Valentine) of Suzdal", "76": "<strong>1.</strong> The most important primary source is the <strong>Minutes of the Council of Bishops of ROAC, 8–12 February 2008, under Metropolitan Valentine, predecessor of Theodore of Suzdal.</strong> These Minutes state expressly that ROAC had decided not to be in communion with the Synod of Metropolitan Vitaly of ROCOR, until the latter breaks communion with the Synod of the Resisters of Cyprian of Fyli. <strong>ROAC justified its stance <u>by characterizing the ecclesiological teaching of the Cyprianites as heretical</u>. <u>(</u>roacusa.org</strong>)<strong>.</strong> Consequently, the Russian Synod had already formulated a clear opposition to Cyprianism, long before the union of the Cyprianites with the Synod of Kallinikos. Primary evidence: <a href=\"https://roacusa.org/Documents/SOBOR_2008_Protocols.html?utm_source=chatgpt.com\"><u>Official Minutes of the Synod of Suzdal of 2008</u></a>", "77": "2. The union of 18 March 2014", "78": "<strong>On 5/18 March 2014 the Synod of Archbishop Kallinikos officially announced the union and incorporation of the Synod of the Resisters into the Church of the G.O.C. of Greece.</strong> This union created an obvious question as to the relationship of the two Synods, because ROAC had previously rejected the ecclesiology of the Cyprianites (<strong>Cyprianism</strong>).", "79": "3. The significance of the synodal condemnation of Cyprianism", "80": "The 2008 Minutes include a special report by <strong>Bishop Andrew of Pavlovsky Posad</strong> on the teaching of Metropolitan Cyprian. <strong>The report characterizes the ecclesiology of the Synod of the Resisters as a covert form of Ecumenism.</strong> The decision constitutes a particularly important piece of evidence for the dogmatic position of ROAC. (roacusa.org)", "81": "The Greek Old Calendarist Synod under Archbishop Gregory", "82": "<a href=\"https://trueorthodoxy.org/polemics/schismatics_kiousites.html?utm_source=chatgpt.com\"><u>GOC Kallinikos - Text of condemnation of his ecclesiastical course</u></a> <strong>This is an express condemnatory position against the synod of Archbishop Kallinikos.</strong>", "83": "BREAKING OF COMMUNION AND REJECTION OF THE SYNOD OF THE CHURCH OF THE G.O.C. OF GREECE UNDER ARCHBISHOP KALLINIKOS SARANTOPOULOS BY A MULTITUDE OF PRIESTS, HOLY MONASTERIES, IMPORTANT PERSONALITIES AND ESPECIALLY BY THE GREAT ROMANIAN SYNOD OF METROPOLITAN EULOGIOS", "84": "<strong>This particular breaking of communion and our walling-off is not an isolated event</strong>, but belongs to a wider series of breakings of communion and rejections of the church of the G.O.C. of Greece (a legal entity under private law), and of the G.O.C. archdiocese of Athens of Archbishop Kallinikos, by many clerics, monks, holy monasteries and laypeople.", "85": "Among the persons and the Ecclesiastical and Monastic communities that <strong>have rejected the Church of the G.O.C.</strong> of Greece, besides <strong>us, the Parish and Administrative Council of the Holy Church of All Saints, the Brotherhood of Saint Mark of Ephesus and the Union of Orthodox Scholars, as presented at length in the text drawn up by the drafting Committee of legal Theologians and Scholars, are:</strong>", "86": "<u><strong>The world-renowned author and historian Mr. Vladimir Moss,</strong></u> <strong>a former champion and friend of the church of the G.O.C. of Greece under Archbishop Kallinikos, who <u>accuses the church of the G.O.C. of Greece of being Sergianist, that is, subjected to the state, through its subjection to the Law on Communities</u> <u>and of being Uniate within the sphere of Resistance and of Confession, for its Uniate tactics, and rejected it and broke off all communion with it.</u></strong> <u> </u>", "87": "<strong>the most pious late-lamented ascetic, the Most God-beloved Bishop of Vresthena, Mr. Theodosios, of the Church of the G.O.C. of Greece,</strong>", "88": "<strong>the Holy Monastery of Saint Stephen the Deep at Aulis,</strong>", "89": "<strong>the most reverent Fr. Demetrios Migdos in Volos,</strong>", "90": "<strong>the distinguished and venerable archimandrite Fr. Agathangelos, now bishop of Samos,</strong>", "91": "<strong>the learned monk and prolific publisher of very many great ecclesiastical works, Fr. Hermolaos of Esphigmenou,</strong>", "92": "<strong>the surgeon known throughout Greece for his struggles for Orthodoxy, Dr. Athanasios Papageorgiou, former director of the Surgical Clinic of Attikon Hospital in Athens,</strong>", "93": "<strong>the Metropolitan of Kalymnos, Mr. Kallinikos, former bishop of the church of the G.O.C. of Greece</strong>", "94": "<strong>the distinguished former Lyceum Principal and teacher of Mathematics, Mr. Athanasios Telonis,</strong>", "95": "<strong>the Professor of the University of Ioannina known throughout Greece, Mr. Demetrios Chatzinikolaou,</strong>", "96": "the pious <strong>Fr. Efstratios Toumparis and several other Presbyters in Piraeus, as well as several clerics of the Metropolis of Thessaloniki under the Bishop of Thessaloniki, Mr. Markopoulos,</strong> and", "97": "<strong>all the chosen brethren of the Parish of the Holy Apostles in Germany together with their Administrative and Parish Council.</strong>", "98": "<strong>The breaking of communion with the church of the G.O.C. of Greece was also carried out by our largest Monastery on Mount Athos, that of the Holy Monastery of Esphigmenou</strong> and several other Zealot Athonite Fathers.", "99": "<strong>Particular mention is made of the largest Romanian, Canonical Old Calendarist Church in the world, under Metropolitan Eulogios, which was in full communion at the time of the breaking of its communion with the church of the G.O.C. of Greece under Archbishop Kallinikos, and which also proceeded to a rejection of the church of the G.O.C., accusing it of heresy as set forth in detail in the present memorandum (decisions and condemnations)!</strong>", "100": "<strong>The Romanian Synod went so far as to anathematize the heretical positions and the bishops and presbyters of the Church of the G.O.C. of Greece who adopt them in practice</strong>.", "101": "<strong>The precise extent and the legal-canonical significance of the breaking of communion with the church of the G.O.C. of Greece emerges from the authentic official Romanian synodal texts - Synodal decisions of the Synod under the late-lamented Metropolitan Demosthenes, and today of the Synod under Metropolitan Eulogios, with certain date, signatures and faithful translation, which are attached among the attached evidence</strong>.", "102": "6. The Romanian sister Orthodox Church literally anathematizes the Church of the G.O.C. of Greece under Archbishop Kallinikos and breaks off all communion with it, <u>accusing in particular two of its bishops as heretics</u> and the church itself as heretical:", "103": "IN CONCLUSION, WE SAY TO ALL THOSE WHO:", "104": "<u>- Regard heretics as part, or as being able to be part, of the Church of Christ,</u>", "105": "<u>- Consider that not every Orthodox synod could judge, <strong>condemn and anathematize heretics without conditions</strong>…</u>", "106": "<u>- Consider that the Church of Christ is not spotless and blameless, <strong>teaching that heretics are or can be members of the Church of Christ,</strong> thereby attacking the holiness of the Church.</u>", "107": "<u>- Consider the Ecumenist, neo-Calvinist and Sergianist</u>", "108": "<u>“churches” to be Orthodox and possessing Holy Grace…</u>", "109": "<u>- <strong>Administer to heretics and schismatics (note: Ecumenists - New Calendarists) the Mystery of the Divine Eucharist,</strong> as if it were useful for their salvation.</u>", "110": "<strong>Have drawn up and support the non-Orthodox teaching called the <em>“theory of the sick member,”</em> which is expressed chiefly through the writing of the text of the <em>“Ecclesiological Positions.”</em></strong>", "111": "<strong>The heresy known as the <em>“Theory of the diseased member,”</em> as well as the work entitled <em>“Ecclesiological Positions,”</em> whose authors and unrepentant supporters essentially claim that the Ecumenist heretics are members of the One, Holy, Sovereign and Apostolic Church until a Great Synod is proclaimed and decides it.</strong>", "112": "Thus all forms of this heresy are also condemned, including the expression of the idea that the Ecumenist heretics (or heretics in general) can be in the One, Holy, Sovereign and Apostolic Church until a Great Synod is convened to pronounce their condemnation.", "113": "<u>ANATHEMA!</u>", "114": "<u>SECRETARIAT OF THE HOLY SYNOD</u>", "115": "5. The Greek Synod under Archbishop Chrysostomos Kiousis - 1986", "116": "Here there is a particularly significant historical element.", "117": "On 5/18 November 1986 the Holy Synod of the G.O.C. of Greece, under Archbishop Chrysostomos Kiousis, condemned Metropolitan Cyprian and his ecclesiology.", "118": "In the synodal act there is included among the hierarchs also <strong>the then Metropolitan of Achaia, Mr. Kallinikos (now archbishop).</strong> True Orthodoxy <a href=\"https://www.trueorthodoxy.org/polemics/heretics_world_orthodoxy_cyprianites_deposition_GOC_1986.html?utm_source=chatgpt.com\"><u>Synodal decision 5/18 November 1986 against the Cyprianites</u></a>", "119": "Its significance is that the union of 2014 was made with an ecclesiastical faction whose ecclesiology had previously been condemned by the very same Greek synodal tradition.", "120": "Which other Russian and Greek bishops condemned the ecclesiology of the Cyprianites concerning sick members and that the Ecumenists retain the priesthood and have sacraments until their final condemnation?", "121": "<strong>The Russian Bishop Gregory Grabbe</strong> (Gregory Grabbe, 1902–1995), of the <strong>Russian Orthodox Church Outside of Russia (ROCOR).</strong> We indeed have an exceptionally important primary synodal piece of evidence, which names <strong>Gregory Grabbe</strong> as a critic of the ecclesiology of Metropolitan Cyprian.", "122": "a. Bishop Gregory Grabbe of the Synod of Metropolitan Vitaly of the Russians of the Diaspora", "123": "In the minutes of the Synod of the <strong>Russian Autonomous Orthodox Church</strong> (ROAC), of January 2008, it is expressly stated that <strong>Gregory Grabbe had rejected the teaching of Cyprian on the possibility of the operation of the Grace of the Holy Spirit in ecclesiastical communities that have become heretical.</strong>", "124": "Moreover, according to the same text, <strong>Bishop Gregory maintained that the acceptance of the Cyprianite heretical ecclesiology by ROCOR brought it into contradiction with its own Anathema against Ecumenism of 1983. roacusa.org</strong>", "125": "b. Bishop Andrew of Pavlovsk", "126": "A second, absolutely documented, hierarch who condemned the ecclesiology of Cyprianism is <strong>Bishop Andrew of Pavlovsk (Andrew of Pavlovskoye).</strong>", "127": "<strong>Bishop Andrew</strong> presented to the Synod of ROAC in 2008 an extensive theological <strong>report against the ecclesiology of Cyprian.</strong>", "128": "His report analyzes and rejects specifically:", "129": "<strong>The theory of <em>“sick members”</em> of the Church.</strong>", "130": "<strong>The view that heretics retain valid Sacraments until their condemnation by a general Synod.</strong>", "131": "The theory that the Church includes two categories of members, the healthy Orthodox and the Ecumenists who are sick in faith.", "132": "The Synod approved the condemnation of this teaching. roacusa.org", "133": "c. Archbishop Andronik Kotliaroff", "134": "There is also a third hierarch, <strong>Archbishop Andronik (Kotliaroff)</strong>, of the Diaspora District of ROCA, who condemned Cyprianism.", "135": "In a text of 17 March 2025, drawn up with the blessing of the bishops of this ecclesiastical group, the teaching of Cyprian on <em><strong>“sick members,”</strong> <strong>valid Mysteries of the Ecumenists</strong> and the <strong>necessity of a future unifying Synod</strong></em> is expressly rejected. <strong>INTERVIEW: Archbishop Andronik (Kotliaroff) of Syracuse and St. Nicholas. On the reasons for the break with Metropolitan Agafangel (Pashkovskiy), lies in the Church, “Cyprianism,” and his canonical status https://rocana.org/# .</strong>", "137": "The text explains that, according to the ecclesiology of the specific Russian jurisdiction, the synodal condemnation ascertains the already accomplished removal from the Church of those who persist in heresy.", "138": "<strong>Another Russian Synod also condemned Cyprianism</strong>", "139": "Decision of the Holy Synod of the Hierarchy of the Orthodox Church of Russia of 4 September 2022", "140": "<strong>Archbishop Stephen (Usachev) of Penza and Central Russia Архиепископ Стефан (Усачев) - подпись Bishop Vladimir - подпись Bishop Vladimir (Matveev) of Voskresensk Епископ Михаил (Платицын) - подпись Bishop Michael (Platitsyn) of Belgorod and Southern Russia</strong>", "141": "<em>…18. To those who affirm and confess the impious ecumenical unbelief of the false-metropolitan Cyprian Koutsoumbas, who affirm the grace of the Mysteries in communities that have broken away from the Church and who impiously taught that heresy is not spiritual death, as the Holy Fathers unanimously decided, but a spiritual illness to which both individual Christians and entire Local Churches can be subject, remaining nevertheless, in part, though sick, in the one Church of Christ: <strong>anathema!</strong></em>", "143": "The condemnation of the Heresy of Cyprianism (1986) by the present Archbishop Kallinikos and the Synod to which he belonged under the late-lamented Archbishop Chrysostomos II", "144": "<strong>All the things mentioned are exactly so and hold true, as is shown also by the decision of the Church of the G.O.C. of Greece under Archbishop Chrysostomos II and his Synod</strong>", "145": "<em>“In addition there is something further that weighs chiefly upon the <strong>Archbishop. Someone must remind him that he has put his signature plainly and broadly, and he can see it and remember, if he has forgotten, on 4 November 1986</strong> (18 November by the New Calendar) <strong>and it was published in the official periodical of the Synod “The Voice of Orthodoxy,” issue 811, January-February 1987, page 23, on the condemnation of the Heresy of Cyprianism, and also on the deposition of Cyprian,</strong> because he, as the Minutes state: <strong>“fell from the Orthodox Faith which the Holy and God-bearing Fathers gave us and from the decisions of the Holy Synod of our Church in the years 1935, 1950 and 1974, and embraced the Ecumenist false doctrines, declaring that the Schismatic New Calendarists constitute the non-innovating One, Holy, Catholic and Apostolic Church, which is the treasury of Salvation, of Grace and the Ark of Salvation, and that the Church of the G.O.C. of Greece is not <u>The Church</u>. Also because he hands over the Holy Mysteries of our Church to Innovating Schismatics and Ecumenist New Calendarists, without any distinction, despite his promises not to do so.”</strong></em>", "146": "<em>Let <strong>His Beatitude</strong> tell us, then, whether he is ready to sign again; otherwise it means that he retracts that signature of his. It is expedient and beneficial to recall all those who signed then:</em>", "147": "<em>“This decision was made known to Metropolitan Antonios of Attica and Megaris, who was not present at the synodal session and expressed his absolute agreement with it and that he too signs this declaration.</em>", "148": "<em><strong>The Holy Synod</strong></em>", "149": "<em><strong>+Archbishop of Athens Chrysostomos</strong></em>", "150": "<em>Gerontios of Piraeus and Salamis</em>", "151": "<em>Kallinikos of Phthiotis and Thaumakos</em>", "152": "<em>Antonios of Attica and Megaris</em>", "153": "<em>Maximos of Demetrias and Magnesia</em>", "154": "<em><strong>Kallinikos of Achaia and Peloponnese</strong></em>", "155": "<em>Matthaios of Oinoe</em>", "156": "<em>Kalliopios of Pentapolis</em>", "157": "<em>Kallinikos of the Dodecanese</em>", "158": "<em>Euthymios of Thessaloniki</em>", "159": "<em>Stephanos of Chios, Psara and Oinousses</em>", "160": "<em>Athanasios of Acharnes and Nea Ionia</em>", "161": "<em>Justin of Euripos and Euboea”</em>", "162": "The preaching in practice of the heresy of Cyprianism by the church of the G.O.C. of Greece and the revival of the heretical teaching of the text of the Cyprianites, anathematized by the sister Canonical Orthodox Romanian Church, <em>“Ecclesiological Positions.”</em>", "163": "The basic and essential problems that concern our Orthodoxy have not been resolved until now. The attempt to shift the matter onto others and onto other, inessential, chiefly procedural matters, on the part of the synodal members of the church of the G.O.C. of Greece, with their childish positions and their foolish accusations against the Orthodox, failed resoundingly, and was also <strong>met with decisive arguments and with the grounding of the positions of our walling-off in the Holy Canons and in the decisions of the Ecumenical and Pan-Orthodox Synods, primarily in the Synodikon of our Orthodoxy, and also in the Unification Text of 2014.</strong>", "164": "The basic problems and <strong>the preaching in practice of the heresy of New Calendarism-Ecumenism by the Bishop of Attica, Mr. Chrysostomos Maniotis, and the Bishop of Thessaloniki, Mr. Markopoulos, were never answered, they remain pending, while the Holy Canons condemn and depose them</strong>:", "165": "<strong>The prearranged and <u>agreed-upon joint celebration</u> - joint ritual-service – concelebration, in a broad sense, of the Bishop of Attica, Mr. Chrysostomos Maniotis, with the Ecumenist-New Calendarist of Ilion, Mr. Athenagoras,</strong> with the acceptance of the festal gifts sent and <strong>the giving in return of a laurel wreath (2024) and an elaborate cross (2026),</strong> as analyzed in detail below.", "166": "<strong>The fraternizing-co-spiritualizing- the cooperation both spiritual and in practice, i.e. <u>the collusion</u> with the heretical Ecumenist-New Calendarist false bishops and false pastors according to Canon 15 of the First-Second Synod</strong>, the <strong>entire tradition of our Fathers,</strong> and also according to the <strong>Unification Text</strong> of 2014, in Thessaloniki, where <strong>the Bishop of Attica, Mr. Chrysostomos Maniotis, attended without his pectoral icon (<i>enkolpion</i>), in practice denying his <em>“archpriestly”</em> status and without a mandate from the synod.</strong>", "167": "<strong>The granting of a portion of the holy relic of the New Martyr Saint Argyrios by the Bishop of Attica, Mr. Maniotis, to the heretical Ecumenist-New Calendarist Mr. Justin of Kalamaria, which refers directly to the Arch-Ecumenist and thoroughly heretical pseudo-patriarch, according to the Holy Canons, Mr. Bartholomew, commemorating him, making a joint supplicatory service with him inside the Bishop of Attica’s monastery. By the commemoration of Mr. Bartholomew Saint Argyrios is insulted and defiled in the province of Mr. Justin, where the holy relic was transferred.</strong>", "168": "<strong>The granting of a platform in the center of the church of Panagia Soumela to the blasphemous and heretical</strong> -(see the statement of the New Calendarist metropolitan of Antinoe)- <strong>and Ecumenist New Calendarist cleric Mr. Vangelis Papanikolaou, where, <u>before the chief secretary of the Synod and the Bishop of Attica, Mr. Chrysostomos Maniotis,</u></strong> <u>he “preached” for quite some time, which is forbidden by the Holy Canons</u> and <strong>the bishop or presbyter who dares to allow these things is deposed and excommunicated.</strong>", "169": "Is it, then, part of the content of Apostolic Faith and Succession <strong>the joint celebration-joint ritual-service-concelebration in a broad sense, with those fallen from the Faith,</strong> as we regard the New Calendarists-Ecumenists in the Unification Text of 2014?", "170": "The fraternizing-meeting and collusion with those fallen from the Orthodox Faith in Thessaloniki <strong>will it not become a model for imitation by others for similar behaviors in the future, when he is amnestied and not deposed, he who is being deposed and excommunicated</strong>, according to the Holy Canons, the Bishop of Attica, Mr. Chrysostomos Maniotis, for his <strong>deviations from the unified line and stance of the Fathers and the orthodox tradition?</strong>", "171": "Will not the donation of a Holy relic by the Bishop of Attica, Mr. Maniotis Chrysostomos, to the heretical New Calendarists-Ecumenists be permitted also in the future, since it remains without condemnation by his Synod?", "172": "Will New Calendarists-Ecumenists be permitted in the future to preach inside our Orthodox Churches, since this was permitted by the Bishop of Attica, Mr. Chrysostomos Maniotis, in the presence of the chief secretary of his Synod, inside the Panagia Soumela?", "173": "Before the false pastors and false bishops Ecumenists-New Calendarists, according to Canon 15 of the First-Second Synod, will the bishops strike the flag of Orthodoxy and appear without a pectoral icon?", "174": "We answer in detail, decisively and with irrefutable arguments, as they were presented and explained on all the issues raised:", "175": "That with Athenagoras of Ilion there took place <strong>a joint celebration, joint ritual-service, concelebration in a broad sense</strong> of the Bishop of Attica, Mr. Chrysostomos Maniotis, on Palm Sunday of 2024. <strong>The same happened also the previous year, 2023, and was repeated in 2026!</strong>", "176": "That in Thessaloniki there was fraternizing, collusion, co-spiritualizing and cooperation of the Bishop of Attica, Mr. Chrysostomos Maniotis, with the New Calendarists-Ecumenists.", "177": "That the donation of a holy Relic to the heretical New Calendarists-Ecumenists, such as to the Ecumenist bishop of Kalamaria Mr. Justin (see attached) by the Bishop of Attica, Mr. Maniotis, is condemned by the Holy Canons and the God-bearing Fathers.", "178": "That in Panagia Soumela there took place an unlawful granting of a Platform for preaching to the untheologized and heretical Ecumenist-New Calendarist, according to the Holy Canons, as he is regarded also by his own bishops and New Calendarist authors, (and also a theatrical cleric!!!), Fr. Vangelis Papanikolaou.", "179": "<strong>That the above actions are condemned by very many Holy Canons and are wider than simple joint prayer and are deposing for those who do them</strong>.", "180": "<strong>That condemnatory and deposing, by the Holy Canons and the Fathers, are not only acts <u>but also omissions,</u></strong> since it is a commonplace and Law of Patristic literature and of secular education that <strong><u>an act consists also in omission.</u></strong>", "181": "That <strong>by the evasion of subsuming the heretical acts of the Bishop of Attica under the decisive Holy Canons it is not possible to acquit the Bishop of Attica, Mr. Maniotis, since they depose and excommunicate him,</strong> and also the attempt to subsume his heretical moves only under the condemnatory, according to the Holy Canons, joint prayer interpreted in the narrow sense, <strong>is provocatively false and is excommunicating-condemnatory also for the one who drew up the relevant texts,</strong> since the notions of joint ritual-service, co-spiritualizing, cooperation, collusion and <strong>concelebration in a broad sense,</strong> are far wider than simple joint prayer, <strong>a condemnation which is readily presumed from the facts of the fraternizing, the collusion and the co-spiritualizing with the heretical Ecumenists-New Calendarists and the recognition in practice of the false bishops of Holy Canon 15 of the First-Second Synod and of the Unification Text as true bishops!</strong>", "182": "<strong>That the Fathers and the Ecumenical Synods condemn and anathematize also those who try to acquit those who preach heretically</strong> as <strong>Saint Theodore the Studite and the Seventh Ecumenical Synod with its Synodikon</strong> teach.", "183": "<strong>The manifestations of Cyprianism in the heretical moves of the Bishop of Attica, Mr. Maniotis, according to the Unification Text of 2014</strong>", "184": "From the Unification Text:", "185": "<em><strong>Par. 9.</strong> In these cases<u>,</u> <strong><u>the essence of the struggle</u></strong> against these anti-evangelical, anti-Orthodox and degenerating phenomena</em> (note: of Ecumenism) <em><u><strong>is not simply and only a potential stance within the framework of a supposed economy, but the cessation of ecclesiastical communion with the Bishop and the Hierarchy is imperatively required forthwith…</strong></u></em>", "186": "<strong>if such heretical behaviors and heretical acts as those of the Bishop of Attica, Mr. Maniotis, are not expressly and categorically condemned, paragraph 9 of the Unification Text is applied exactly, which reads as follows:</strong>", "187": "<em><strong>which introduces</strong> (<u>indeed</u> <strong>synodically) </strong></em><strong>{note: if such heretical behavior is not expressly condemned, the heretical text <em>“Ecclesiological Positions”</em> of the Cyprianites by his Synod, which has first, however, been cleansed of the taint of the heresy of Cyprianism and of its three bishops accused by the Romanians as heretics, as set forth} <em>heresy into the Church, whether by preaching it, <u>or by contributing to its spread through silence, passivity or indifference.</u> </em></strong>", "188": "This will happen, <strong>then, if the Synod keeps silent before the denounced heretical moves and the heresy of New Calendarism-Ecumenism preached in practice by the Bishop of Attica, Mr. Maniotis- (Canon 15 of the First-Second Synod will be applied, as several have already applied it against the church of the G.O.C. of Greece.</strong>", "189": "The above text and paragraph 10 below of the <strong>Unification Text leaves no doubt about the obligation of the Synod and of all the faithful and the so-called Canonical, to break communion with the one who preaches heretically,</strong> since, according to the Text, <strong><u>the cessation of ecclesiastical communion with the Bishop and the Hierarchy is imperatively required forthwith in such cases:</u></strong>", "190": "<em><strong>Par. 10.</strong> The Walling-Off from the fallen pastors, who are now characterized as <strong>“false bishops”</strong> and <strong>“false teachers,”</strong> constitutes <strong>a most necessary obligation</strong> of the genuine Orthodox in a time of heresy, for the safeguarding of <u>the <strong>Uniqueness,</strong> the <strong>Unity</strong> and the <strong>Catholicity</strong> of the Church, for confessional <strong>Witness of Faith,</strong> but also for a missionary saving <strong>Call to Repentance to those who go astray and to those who commune with them.</strong></u></em> <u> </u>", "191": "Chapter 6. The Return to Genuine Orthodoxy", "192": "<em><strong>1.</strong> In the reception of repentant heretics and schismatics, the Ecumenical and Local Synods of the Church, besides the <strong>principle of Strictness (<i>akribeia</i>),</strong> applied from time to time also the so-called <strong>principle of Economy (<i>oikonomia</i>),</strong> that is, a Canonical and Pastoral practice according to which it is possible for a <strong>temporary deviation</strong> from the letter of the Holy Canons to occur, without violating their spirit.</em>", "193": "<em><strong>2.</strong> Nevertheless, <strong>Economy</strong> can <strong>never,</strong> of course, and <strong>in no case permit the amnesty of any sin or any compromise regarding the “Right and Saving Confession of the Faith,”</strong> inasmuch as <strong>Economy</strong> looks purely and solely, in a spirit of philanthropic condescension, to the facilitation of the salvation of souls, for whom Christ died.</em>", "194": "<em><strong>3.</strong> The application of <strong>Economy in the admission</strong> of heretics and schismatics into Ecclesiastical Communion <strong>in no way means that the Church recognizes the validity and the existence of their mysteries,</strong> performed <strong>outside Her Canonical and Charismatic Boundaries.</strong></em>", "195": "That is, of the New Calendarists - Ecumenists, if they wish to return to the Church, since, as is noted in the Unification Text, New Calendarism and Ecumenism are condemned heresies. New Calendarism both by the Synods of 1583, 1587 and 1592, and Ecumenism in 1983 by Saint Philaret and his Synod, by the Synod of the church of the G.O.C. of Greece under our ever-memorable Archbishop Chrysostomos Kiousis in 1998, and by the Canonical and sister Romanian Church in 2013.", "196": "<em><strong>Chap. 7. Par. 5.</strong> This necessity becomes understandable from the fact that the true Church, as the real Body of Christ, is by Her very nature <strong>Catholic</strong> in the fullness of Truth, of Grace and of Salvation, and <strong>pronounces synodically through Her Bishops</strong> against heterodox teachings and the worldwide scandal arising from them; consequently, She <strong>ought to pursue</strong> on the one hand the <strong>formulation</strong> of the Truths of the Faith, for the demarcation of Truth from falsehood, and on the other the <strong>denunciation</strong> and <strong>condemnation</strong> of error and of the corruption from heresy and heretics, for the protection of the Flock, <u> <strong>ascertaining</strong> and <strong>proclaiming the already existing fall of the heretics.</strong> </u></em>", "197": "<u>The New Calendarists and Ecumenists, according to what is stated in the above Unification Text, <strong>have already fallen, “<em>the fall of the heretics exists,”</em></strong></u> <strong>according to the precise description of the Text,</strong> so that <strong><u>a future Synod will do nothing other than to ascertain the already existing fall of the heretics,</u></strong> according to the Unification Text, and in accordance with the entire teaching of the God-bearing Fathers!", "198": "Therefore also the Bishop of Attica, Mr. Maniotis, <strong>by his fraternizing with the heretical Ecumenist New Calendarists in Athens and in Thessaloniki, by his acceptance, from the Ecumenist-New Calendarist of Ilion, Mr. Athenagoras, of the festal gifts sent and his joint celebration with the false pastor of the Unification Text of 2014, showed, <u>and indeed by his offering of a laurel wreath to this Ecumenist,</u> <em><u>who has fallen from the Orthodox Faith,</u></em></strong> <u><strong>according to the Unification Text,</strong> and according to the Fathers, that he thought and thinks the same as he, <strong>confusing the Canon of the Church and setting an example for the other bishops, priests and faithful,</strong></u> <strong>that there is no difference between the Orthodox and the Ecumenists-New Calendarists and that we are the same, disregarding the struggles, the persecutions, the defrockings of the pure levites, the exiles and imprisonments of our priests and of our hierarchs and the blood that was shed at Mandra in defense of the Patristic and the Orthodox Festal Calendar. And by the other heretical acts of his mentioned, and to be mentioned below, he certified it repeatedly, finally and irrevocably!</strong>", "199": "Since, indeed, he remained unrepentant for a long period of time, about five months, despite the exhortations to take down his controversial posts, proclaiming through the electronic press in practice the heresy of Ecumenism-New Calendarism, <strong>keeping posted for five months on his official website the heretical acts (in 2024), and in the current year (2026), for which he was accused, there applied and applies also to him that of the God-speaking Apostle Paul</strong>:", "200": "<strong>To (Titus 3:8-15),</strong> <em>10 <strong>A man that is an heretick after the first and second</strong> <strong>admonition reject</strong>; 11 knowing that he that is such <strong><u>is subverted, and sinneth, being condemned of himself</u></strong></em>! <em><strong>(“is subverted (<i>exestraptai</i>) such a one”</strong></em> from the verb EKSTREPHO = TO WORSEN, TO BE DISGRACED... subverted means disgraced... <strong>the dictionary of Papyros explains the word of the Apostle).</strong>", "201": "<u>And after the joint supplicatory service with Mr. Justin of Kalamaria, and indeed at night,</u> inside the monastery of the Bishop of Attica, where there was undoubtedly joint prayer, and the donation of a relic to the Great Ecumenist Mr. Justin, who also organized an event for the proclaimed freemason and great Ecumenist Athenagoras, where he extols him, the trilogy of the tragic falls of the Bishop of Attica was completed. (See also the relevant, publicly known, video of channel 4 that circulates widely on the internet).", "202": "And the sermon of the New Calendarist cleric Mr. Vangelis Papanikolaou inside the Panagia Soumela, where he was also given a microphone and spoke for a long time in the center of the Church, extolling the Bishop of Attica for the twenty-five years of his episcopate, on the day of the feast of Saint Kassandra, <u>stressing that what he says he does not say without the blessing of his New Calendar bishop, is also an act that draws deposition upon the Bishop of Attica.</u>", "203": "<strong>The heretics are dead.</strong>", "204": "They cannot act in the name of the Catholic Church, <strong>because they blaspheme the All-Holy Spirit.</strong> This is what the Athonite Fathers teach us, <strong>those who were martyred under the Latin-minded Bekkos.</strong> This is what <strong>the Greatest of the Theologians, Saint Nikodemos the Athonite,</strong> teaches us regarding the Iconoclasts, <strong><u>of a deadening already existing</u></strong>, before their complete recognition and diagnosis-condemnation by the Seventh Ecumenical Synod:", "205": "<strong>The footnote to Apostolic Canon 3,</strong> which requires the second person in order to activate the penalty of the Canon, that is, for the legal consequence of the Holy Canon to ensue, refers to individual bishops, <strong><u>who pre-eminently commit Canonical violations</u></strong> and <strong><u>not to matters of faith!</u></strong>", "206": "Since, then, in the present case it concerns an individual bishop in principle liable to trial, a trial and condemnation by the Church is required, <em>Holy Pedalion,</em> footnote 1 on Apostolic Canon 3, pp. 4-5, Thessaloniki 1982, exact reprint of the third edition of 1864:", "207": "<em>“The Canons command the Synod of the living Bishops to depose priests, or to excommunicate, or to anathematize the laity, where they transgress the Canons. However, if the Synod does not actually carry out the deposition of the priests, or the excommunication, or anathematization of the laity, these priests, and the laity, are neither deposed in actuality, nor excommunicated or anathematized. They are liable, however, here to deposition and excommunication or anathematization, and there to the divine judgment… Hence those foolish people greatly err who say that in the present times all those ordained contrary to the canons are in actuality deposed. A priest-accusing tongue is that which chatters such words, not understanding that the command of the Canons, without the actual operation of the second person, namely the synod, is incomplete, not operating immediately and before judgment of itself. These very divine Apostles clearly explain themselves by their 46th Canon, since they do not say that whatever Bishop or Presbyter receives the baptism of heretics is immediately in actuality deposed, but we command that he be deposed, that is, that he be brought to judgment, and if it is proved that he did this, then let him be stripped of the priesthood by your own decision, this we command.”</em>", "208": "In the specific violations, however, as they were set out in detail above, of the Bishop of Attica, Mr. Chrysostomos Maniotis, <u>the things done by him and the factual circumstances are regarded as fully proved, since the publication of his deeds was made by himself and constitutes a confession, which means full proof, a counter-proof not being permitted (the announcement was made also by a multitude of other public websites and printed media)!</u>", "209": "Therefore the:", "210": "<strong>if it is proved, according to the above, of the greatest teacher Saint Nikodemos</strong>", "211": "<strong>it is already completely proved,</strong>", "212": "<strong>the factual circumstances are fully proved and</strong>", "213": "<strong>no trial is required as to <em>“how he did this”! </em></strong>", "214": "What remains is the evaluation of the facts completely proved through the confession by the Bishop of Attica, Mr. Chrysostomos himself, as to which canonical penalties will be imposed on him, <u>after, however, the synod “church of the G.O.C. of Greece,” a recognized association, legal entity under private law, has purified itself of the heretical elements and expels the bishops accused of heresy,</u> and when and if it is legalized by the State, and it becomes possible to establish lawfully an ecclesiastical court. Until then the Bishop of Attica, Mr. Maniotis Chrysostomos, is excommunicate and the faithful people has already deposed and anathematized him.", "216": "<strong>The Identity of the Adherents of the Heresy of Cyprianism</strong>", "217": "From the Secretariat of the Holy Synod of the Resisters<br/>on 2 October 2006 (Old Style)", "218": "The Orthodox Resistance against the ecclesiological heresy of syncretistic Ecumenism", "219": "Basic Ecclesiological and Canonical Positions", "220": "“For it is the command of the Lord not to keep silent in a time when the Faith is in danger; for speak, he says, and hold not thy peace...”", "221": "Saint Theodore the Studite, PG vol. 99, col. 1321AB", "222": "a. The identity of the Holy Synod of the Resisters", "223": "1. The Holy Synod of the Resisters, with the help of God and the protection of the Theotokos, shepherds those pious Orthodox Christians who are in principle Anti-ecumenists and follow the Patristic Ecclesiastical Calendar, constituting the Ecclesiastical <strong>Community</strong> of the Anti-ecumenists of the Patristic Calendar.", "224": "2. The pious Anti-ecumenists have broken, since the year 1924, sacramental communion with the so-called official Churches, which take part in the Ecumenical Movement and have adopted or tolerate the New Calendar, because they regard <strong>Ecumenism</strong> as an ecclesiological <strong>heresy</strong>, and <strong>the New Calendar</strong> as a condemned <strong>innovation</strong>.", "225": "3. The work of the Holy Synod of the Resisters is fundamentally unifying, inasmuch as it aims at informing the pious about the heretical character of the Ecumenical Movement.", "226": "4. Serious and responsible information on this matter will awaken, God willing, the synodal conscience of the Orthodox Church, toward the convening of a General Synod of Union in the Truth of the Faith, so that the heresy may be condemned and the festal unity <strong>of the Orthodox</strong> may be restored.", "227": "b. Non-Innovators and Walling-Off", "228": "1. The whole body of Anti-ecumenists, who turned away from <strong>the innovation of Ecumenism</strong> and of the New Calendar, by this stance of theirs, that is, of their walling-off 1 from the Innovators, did not cause a Schism in the Church, but obeyed Her and remained united with Her.", "229": "2. The Holy Fathers and the Holy Canons praise and call blessed those who wall themselves off, that is, separate from innovating pastors for dogmatic reasons, when these publicly preach false doctrines and heresies<sup>1</sup>.", "230": "3. The sin of Schism exists exclusively and solely in the case in which a part of the clergy and the people breaks relation and communion with the canonical Pastors of the Church “without cause” and “without reason,” invoking “curable matters” or personal transgressions of the hierarchs<sup>2</sup>.", "231": "4. The heresy of Ecumenism, from which the innovation of the New Calendar flowed, cannot be regarded and characterized as a “curable matter,” inasmuch as it has undergone in many ways and manners a deep theological anatomy and has justly and validly been characterized as “something much worse than pan-heresy” and as “a sickness unto death,”<sup>3</sup> as “the most abominable syncretism” and as “worse than every heresy,”<sup>4</sup> and finally as “unheard-of betrayal.”<sup>5</sup>", "232": "5. Consequently, those who follow the Patristic Ecclesiastical Calendar and are Anti-ecumenists are not only not Schismatics, but constitute <strong>the Non-Innovating Fullness of the Orthodox Church</strong>, which <strong>has walled itself off</strong> lawfully and canonically <strong>from the Innovators and resists</strong> in a manner pleasing to God,<sup>6</sup> that is, <strong>struggles for the</strong> pacification and <strong>unity of the Church.</strong>", "233": "c. The Calendar and Ecumenism", "234": "1. The unbreakable relation between the Ecumenical Movement and the Calendar Reform is absolutely documented, theologically and historically, to the point of proving that a relation of causality exists between them.", "235": "2. The sources testify that the Reformers of 1924 had given the Calendar matter a most clear ecumenist dimension, inasmuch as", "236": "a. they acted with the feeling that they constituted “members of the pan-Christian brotherhood”;", "237": "b. they deliberated with the conviction that “the hour has come for the renewed restoration of the unity of Christians at least on this point”;", "238": "c. they sought the “service of pan-Christian unity”;", "239": "d. they aimed at the “rapprochement of the two Christian worlds of East and West in the celebration of the great Christian feasts”;", "240": "e. they regarded the New Calendar as “the first stone for the edifice of the union of all the churches of God.”<sup>7</sup>", "241": "3. Likewise, the direct relation Ecumenism-Calendar was fully known to the Reformer of 1924, that is, to Archbishop of Athens Chrysostomos Papadopoulos himself (+ 1938), who not only had consciously embraced the precondition of the Reform, that is, the ecumenist Encyclical of 1920 of the Patriarchate of Constantinople, but had also cooperated with the innovator Meletios Metaxakis in its prospects, so that Chrysostomos Papadopoulos is regarded today as a pioneer Ecumenist and as one of the founders of the World Council of Churches.<sup>8</sup>", "242": "d. Syncretistic Ecumenism", "243": "1. The heretical and syncretistic character of Ecumenism has been ascertained and publicly proclaimed by a cloud of eminent persons, so that from 1920 (and especially 1924) onward, the stance toward this pan-heresy is indisputably the criterion and the touchstone of the orthodoxy of each person.", "244": "2. The ever-memorable University Professor Andreas Theodorou (+ 2004) described Ecumenism as <em>“something much worse than pan-heresy”; “Ecumenism is a transgression, an amnesty, a disregard, not to say legitimization and justification of heresies”; “Ecumenism in the sacred sphere of Orthodoxy is a sickness unto death!”;</em>", "245": "<em>“Ecumenism, this fearsome beast of the Apocalypse, the two-headed ecclesiological monster, constricts suffocatingly with its tentacles the whole immaculate Body of Orthodoxy. The danger looming from the latter is perhaps the greatest in the history of the Orthodox Church.”<sup>9</sup></em>", "246": "3. The late-lamented University Professor <strong>Konstantinos Mouratidis</strong> (+ ) had declared categorically that <em>“in the sphere of the World Council of Churches,</em> [this foremost institutional organ of the Ecumenical Movement], <em>there takes place what is most categorically by the teaching”</em> of the Holy Fathers <em>“excluded and condemned, namely cooperation between Orthodoxy and Heresy and correspondingly between Orthodox and Heretics on matters of Faith, such as the cooperative drafting of theological texts and the joint participation in worship gatherings and the joint representation of the Christian religion on the great problems of humanity, etc.”;</em> and all these constitute <em>“a flagrant violation of divinely inspired holy Canons and of fundamental ecclesiastical Principles, <strong>by which the very essence and the general redemptive course of Orthodoxy is struck</strong>”</em>.<sup>10</sup>", "247": "4. The recent <em>“Inter-Orthodox Conference of Thessaloniki”</em> (20-24.9.2004), which had as its theme: <em>“Ecumenism: Genesis-Expectations-Disappointments,”</em> after about sixty Reports, in its Conclusions characterized Ecumenism, Inter-Christian and Inter-religious, as “pan-heresy,” as the <em>“greatest ecclesiological heresy in the history of the Church,” “with most grave soteriological consequences”</em> and proclaimed that <em>“inter-religious meetings and inter-religious dialogues have led to impermissible syncretism.”</em><sup>11</sup>", "248": "e. The division of the Anti-ecumenists", "249": "1. In the holy resistance against syncretistic Ecumenism, the Orthodox Anti-ecumenists of the Patristic Calendar, by the permission of God, have been divided into various non-communing ecclesiastical Communities, because chiefly they do not have a common ecclesiological self-consciousness.", "250": "2. Part of the pious of the Patristic Calendar has deviated into a sterile anti-New Calendarism, while others have fenced themselves in, adopting an anti-theological introversion, which led them to the proclamation of the ecclesiological and soteriological exclusivity of their Community.", "251": "3. The Holy Synod of the Resisters in principle (<i>in principio</i>) regards as desirable the cooperation and further the union of itself with those of the Communities of the Patristic Calendar which, however, by all means fulfill the criteria of valid ecclesiastical bodies.", "252": "4. Nevertheless, it is judged that this cooperation, in the prospect of the union of the Communities of the Patristic Calendar of varied origins, is for the present not feasible, inasmuch as first and foremost there prevails an unprecedented confusion of theological criteria, and chiefly there exists the unbridgeable chasm of ecclesiological otherness.", "253": "5. This stance is based on the conviction that an indispensable precondition of every unifying effort within the Patristic Calendar is the full clarification of the following two critical matters:", "254": "a. <strong>the position of the as yet unjudged heretics and of those in communion with them, such as the innovating Ecumenists, in the Body of the Church</strong><sup>12</sup>;", "255": "b. the criteria for ascertaining valid ecclesiastical bodies, inasmuch as the dissolution of every theological, canonical and moral barrier, on the pretext of the struggle against the ecumenist Innovation, a phenomenon unfortunately already most common, dissolves every notion of ecclesiastical authority and prevents every unifying prospect.", "256": "6. It is recalled indicatively that <strong>Saint Theodore the Studite</strong>, referring ad hoc to this matter, determines with absolute patristic documentation, “according to all the Saints,” the marks of the “unimpeachable” and “uncondemned” Cleric with whom the resisting Orthodox ought, in a time of heretical confusion, to have communion,", "257": "a. because, according to the Saint, heresy is not the only obstacle to communion; there are other obstacles too: those of a canonical nature, as also those “suspected and heard of as faulty in the course of life”;", "258": "b. because the canonical obstacles and the “manifestly” “faulty in the course of life,” “even if secondary,” in relation to heresy, are “yet not lesser for those who consider piously,” inasmuch as “the one is struck by the other”;", "259": "c. because the so timely patristic exhortation remains in force also today: <em>“Inquire, be diligent; for uninvestigated communion is not without danger; for the danger is over great matters”</em> (of Saint Chrysostom); <em>“(let us)</em>", "260": "<em>therefore seek out and be diligent about from whom we ought to commune.”</em><sup>13</sup>", "261": "Toward peace and unity", "262": "1. The vision of pacification and <strong>of the reunification of the divided Orthodox, Anti-ecumenists and Ecumenists</strong>, in the prospect, moreover, of the simultaneous healing of the much-fragmented Communities of the Patristic Calendar, requires the following three specific, drastic and saving, healing actions on the part of the Innovators, in humility and repentance and on the basis of Patristic Orthodoxy:", "263": "a. To proclaim the exclusiveness (<i>exclusiveness</i>) of Orthodox Ecclesiology and Soteriology;", "264": "b. To renounce the syncretistic Ecumenical Movement, as well as the comprehensiveness (<i>comprehensiveness</i>) of ecumenist ecclesiology, and at the same time to withdraw from all its institutional Organs.", "265": "c. To restore the festal unity of the Orthodox, through the return to the “Julian calendar, which has been kept from the ages in the Orthodox Church,” inasmuch as this was always regarded “as the only one befitting the Church,” “because it is patristic and has been ecclesiastically sanctioned from of old.”<sup>14</sup>", "266": "2. The gravely and exclusively guilty ones <strong>of the</strong> tragic <strong>division of the Orthodox</strong>, and of course of all its consequences, <strong>are the innovating Ecumenists</strong>, who should take up, while there is yet time, their responsibilities, because according to Saint Chrysostom: <em>“nothing so provokes God as the division of the Church”</em> and <em>“not even the blood of martyrdom can wipe out this sin.”</em><sup>15</sup>", "267": "From the Secretariat<br/>of the Holy Synod of the Resisters<br/>on 2 October 2006 (Old Style)<br/>† Holy Martyrs Cyprian and Justina", "268": "Notes", "269": "1. <strong>First-Second Holy Synod, Holy Canon 15.</strong>", "270": "2. <strong>Holy Apostles, Holy Canon 31</strong>; First-Second Holy Synod, Holy Canon 15; <strong>Basil the Great,</strong> Holy Canon 1. See also the Commentaries on the Holy Canons in question.", "271": "3. <strong>Andreas Theodorou,</strong> <em>Orthodoxy Yesterday and Today,</em> p. 21, publications of <strong>“Orthodoxos Typos,”</strong> Athens 1973.", "272": "4. <strong>Archim. Epiphanios Theodoropoulos,</strong> Articles-Studies-Letters, vol. 1, pp. 163-164, Athens 1981.", "273": "5. <strong>Archim. Justin Popović,</strong> <em>“An Orthodox Opinion and Testimony,”</em> periodical <strong>“Koinonia,”</strong> March-April 1975, pp. 95-101.", "274": "6. <strong>Saint Theodore the Studite,</strong> PG vol. 99, col. 1045D, <em>Epistle 39, To Theophilos the Abbot,</em> E.L.I.", "275": "7. <strong>Dionysios M. Batistatos</strong> (ed.), <em>Minutes and Decisions of the Pan-Orthodox Congress in Constantinople</em> (10.5-8.6.1923), pp. 72, 14, 6, 57 and 189, Athens 1982.", "276": "8. <strong>Antonios M. Papadopoulos,</strong> <em>“The Stance of the Church of Greece toward the Relations of the Orthodox Church with the Heterodox,”</em> in <em><strong>Witness and Ministry of Orthodoxy Today,</strong></em> vol. 2, pp. 85-87, Kyriakidis Brothers publications, Thessaloniki 1998; Archim. <strong>Theoklitos A. Strangas,</strong> <em><strong>History of the Church of Greece</strong></em>..., vol. 2, pp. 901-914, Athens 1970.", "277": "9. Andreas Theodorou, ibid., pp. 21 and 23.", "278": "10. <strong>Konstantinos Dor. Mouratidis,</strong> Ecumenical Movement - The great contemporary temptation of Orthodoxy, pp. 71-72 and 87, publications of “Orthodoxos Typos,” Athens 1973.", "279": "11. <strong>“Inter-Orthodox Conference of Thessaloniki”</strong> (20-24.9.2004), Conclusions, newspaper “Orthodoxos Typos,” no. 1577/17.12.2004, p. 5; periodical “Theodromia,” October-December 2004, pp. 504-521; periodical “Parakatatheke,” no. 38/ September-October 2004, pp. 2-12.", "280": "12. See our study: “The position of the as yet unjudged heretics in the Church,” periodical “Orthodox Resistance and Witness,” 2nd series, no. 1/ January 2000, pp. 19-36.", "281": "13. See <strong>Saint Theodore the Studite,</strong> PG vol. 99, col. 1101-1108, <strong>Epistle 53, To Stephen the reader and those with him</strong>, E.L.I.", "282": "14. <strong>Vasileios Th. Stavridis - Evangelia A. Varella,</strong> <em>History of the Ecumenical Movement,</em> p. 325, <em>Patriarchal and Synodal Encyclical of 1902,</em> publications “P.I.P.M.,” Analekta Vlatadon - 47, Thessaloniki 1996.", "283": "15. Saint Chrysostom, PG vol. 62, col. 85/To the Ephesians, Homily 11, § 4.", "284": "THE CONTROVERSIAL PARTS OF THE POSITIONS OF THE CYPRIANITES THAT NEVER CHANGED IN PRACTICE, REPREACHED EVERYWHERE IN GREECE AND ABROAD, OF THE CONDEMNED HERESY OF CYPRIANISM BY THE SYNOD OF THE CHURCH OF THE G.O.C. OF GREECE AND THE BISHOP OF ATTICA MR. MANIOTIS CHRYSOSTOMOS, WITH RELEVANT COMMENTS", "285": "The Holy Synod of the Resisters shepherds those who constitute the Ecclesiastical <strong>Community (not the Church of Christ)</strong> of the Anti-ecumenists.", "286": "The work is fundamentally unifying, toward the convening of a General Synod of Union, so that the heresy may be condemned and the festal unity <strong>of the Orthodox</strong> may be restored.", "287": "<strong>(Here by Orthodox they also mean the Heretical Ecumenist New Calendarists)</strong>", "288": "<strong>the innovation of Ecumenism (here it is Innovation not Heresy)</strong>", "289": "constitute <strong>the Non-Innovating Fullness of the Orthodox Church</strong>, which <strong>has walled itself off</strong> lawfully and canonically <strong>from the Innovators and resists</strong> in a manner pleasing to God 6, that is, <strong>struggles for the</strong> pacification and <strong>unity of the Church.</strong>", "290": "<strong>That is, the Church, because of the walling-off, is divided into Innovators and Non-Innovators and they are trying to unite the two parts of it.</strong>", "291": "an indispensable precondition of every unifying effort within the Patristic Calendar is the full clarification of the following two critical matters:", "292": "a. <strong>the position of the as yet unjudged heretics (as if they were preaching a newly-appeared heresy) and of those in communion with them, such as the Innovating Ecumenists, in the Body of the Church. Here the multi-heretical New Calendarist Ecumenist adherents and communicants of condemned heresies are simply innovators and, most important, are within the body of the Church of Christ.</strong>", "293": "The vision of pacification and <strong>of the reunification of the divided Orthodox, Anti-ecumenists and Ecumenists, And here the Multi-heretical Ecumenist New Calendarists are Orthodox.</strong>", "294": "The gravely and exclusively guilty ones <strong>of the</strong> tragic <strong>division of the Orthodox, and of course of all its consequences, are the Innovating Ecumenists And here the Ecumenists, from Heretics become Innovators again - they supposedly preach something newfangled – but they are also Orthodox.</strong>", "295": "<strong>The Ecclesiastical Union of the Orthodox Community of the Resisters with the Church of the Genuine Orthodox Christians. Objections-Concerns, Transgression-</strong>", "296": "Refutation by us of this untheologized and heretical text", "297": "On p. 5 (a2) it says:", "298": "<em><strong>“the former Resisters have withdrawn, which they did even from their official Website, their earlier formulated ecclesiological formulations;”</strong></em>", "299": "At this point they say that they have withdrawn them, not that they have refuted them.", "300": "On p. 6 it says:", "301": "<em><strong>“they took up their responsibilities in repentance for the schism and its consequences from 1984 onward.”</strong></em>", "302": "This is very general and vague, without evidence for the repentance they mention, which ought to have been public with a renunciation of the heresy of Cyprianism.", "303": "On p. 6 (b1) it says:", "304": "<em><strong>“There never existed a heresy called Cyprianism and our Holy Synod never officially used this term;</strong></em>", "305": "they deliberately write “existed,” to show that it concerned the past and has now ceased. That is, even if it existed, it does not exist today. Of course the name did not pre-exist either, since it is their own brand name. Nevertheless they say that they did not use this term officially, but in particular they do not write that they exclude it.", "306": "On p. 6 (b1) it says: <em>“the former Resisters not only had not preached</em>", "307": "<em><strong>officially-synodically what was attributed to them as Cyprianism,”</strong></em>", "308": "Here we laugh to tears. An enormous lie! Countless are their texts in periodicals, videos, and so many condemnations and anathemas besides that they received, precisely, for what they had preached officially and <u>Synodically</u> and was attributed to them as Cyprianism.", "309": "On p. 6 (b1) it says:", "310": "<em><strong>“as for example the supposed regarding of the official Church as Mother Church, but they also clearly opposed these things, and indeed during the Unification Process.”</strong></em>", "311": "(The entire heretical Ecclesiology of the resistance means and describes this and revolves around it, regardless of whether it does not constantly mention the word Mother. The text of the former Resisters that follows, does it perhaps mean something else?", "312": "<em><strong>“Those who have walled themselves off and resist from the Patristic Calendar do not constitute an administrative substitute of the Innovating Church, nor a parallel to the New Calendarist jurisdiction, nor a second Orthodox Church in Greece, but belong to the Patristic and Non-Innovating Church of Greece,…”</strong></em>", "313": "<strong>On p. 6, on the yellow background it says<em>: “Moreover, ecclesiological formulations of the former Resisters in the past, which of course our Church condemned,</em></strong> <em><strong>”</strong></em>", "314": "(Here there is the admission that our Church in the past condemned the Synod of the Resisters for the heresy of Cyprianism, whereas in the text above they had denied, saying: <em>“had not preached officially-synodically what was attributed to them as Cyprianism,”</em>", "315": "On p. 6, on the yellow background it says:", "316": "<em>“were not expressed stubbornly, dogmatically and definitively, in which case they would indeed constitute a heresy, and indeed an eponymous one, but as ‘thoughts for reflection and discussion.’”</em>", "317": "Here we really observe an admission of unrepentance, because even at these moments of submission, of effort to agree on accession and incorporation into the Church and the signing of the Unification Text, the former Resisters show that they have not changed their ecclesiological positions. The author writes that they insist on expressing their heretical positions, but not with much stubbornness lest they be characterized also as heretics by name. They express their heretical positions only indirectly, as <em>“thoughts for reflection and discussion.”</em>", "318": "That is, truly, we have no need of witnesses for this mockery!", "319": "On p. 7 in (c2) <em>“We remind that also in the past there were similar Acts on the deceased, although they were burdened not only with deposition, but with anathematization,”</em>", "320": "(here they mean and admit the deposition of Cyprian in 1986)", "321": "On p. 7 in (c3)", "322": "<em><strong>“The late-lamented Metropolitan Cyprian had clearly expressed his desire for the restoration of his communion with our Holy Synod, against which –it should be noted– he never worked, nor intended to substitute it,”</strong></em>", "323": "Such a desire by Cyprian, demonstrably formulated, we do not know of; if it exists, however, even unofficially, let it be submitted. As for how much he <u>worked against</u> <u>the Martyric Church of the G.O.C. of Greece</u>, even the stones know it. His official characterization of the True Church of the G.O.C. was <em>COUNTER-SYNAGOGUE.</em> As for the claim that he <em><u>did not intend</u> to substitute it,</em> he did exactly the opposite, establishing his own Synod.)", "324": "On p. 7 in (c3) <em>“and our Synod had taken decisions against him in the year 1986, because chiefly he established his own Synod, although –as the former Resisters assure us– it had a provisional character in the prospect of the Union.”</em>", "325": "(It is a lie that he was deposed because chiefly he established his own Synod.", "326": "The truth about the accusations, in order of gravity, was:", "327": "A). Because: They fell from the Orthodox Faith, which the Holy and God-bearing Fathers of the Church gave us and the decisions of the Holy Synods of our Church, of the years 1935, 1950, and 1974, and embraced Ecumenist false doctrines, according to which, the schismatic New Calendarists make up the traditional One, Holy, Catholic and Apostolic Church, which is a treasury and Ark of salvation, and that our Church of the True Orthodox Christians is not the Church.<br>", "328": "B). Because they give the Holy Mysteries of the Church, without distinction and examination, to the Innovating schismatics and Ecumenist New Calendarists.", "329": "C). Because they cut themselves off from our Church and established their own altar and the so-called <em>“Holy Synod of the Resisters,”</em> with members of this synod the Metropolitans, Cyprian of Oropos and John of Sardinia and those who were uncanonically ordained by them and who make up the other accused. – Periodical: <em>“The Voice of Orthodoxy,”</em> Issue 811", "330": "January-February 1987, page 23).", "331": "The other claim, that the Synod they established <em>“had a provisional character in the prospect of the Union,”</em> after about 30 years of existence, until the death of Cyprian, let us regard at least as a joke!", "332": "Besides, their real prospect and their vision is recorded officially also in the printed text: <em>The Orthodox Resistance against the ecclesiological heresy of syncretistic Ecumenism - Basic Ecclesiological and Canonical Positions -</em> of 2 October 2006 (O.S.), p. 6 col. 1, where word for word they speak of:", "333": "<em>“The vision of pacification and of the reunification of the divided Orthodox, Anti-ecumenists and Ecumenists,</em> (that is, here too they tell us that the Ecumenists are Orthodox)…", "334": "On p. 7 in (c4) <em>“The accusation concerning Ecumenism, which was indeed connected with the reported conviction of the late-lamented Metropolitan Cyprian about the official Church as Mother Church, is completely refuted by the following public confirmation of the former Resisters of the year 2008:</em> (So until 2008 this accusation held; otherwise, how are his so many condemnations from 1986 onward explained).", "335": "<em>“This truly unapproved expression, used once by a Bishop of ours and already withdrawn by him as ill-aimed, never constituted an official synodal proclamation of us the Resisters, nor was it ever used, much less was it incorporated into basic and fundamental texts, expressing our ecclesiological and anti-ecumenist self-consciousness.”</em>", "336": "(They do not tell us, however, by which Bishop it was used, nor when and by what document it was withdrawn. The meaning of this expression concerning the official Church as Mother Church, is diffused in very many texts of the Ecclesiological positions of the Resisters, from which the above were cited quite offhand.", "337": "On p. 7", "338": "<em><strong>“The accusation concerning the provision of mysteries by the late-lamented Metropolitan Cyprian indiscriminately to laity of the Innovation, is now baseless, inasmuch as the former Resisters, following also their Synodal Decision of years ago, officially published indeed, exclude from Holy Communion those who do not belong to the Church of the Genuine Orthodox Christians.”</strong></em>", "339": "(Those who are eyewitnesses know it. They do not tell us when the decision was issued which supposedly <em>“is now baseless,”</em> and that at least until then it was officially well-founded, so that until then they were justly accused).", "340": "Likewise in the expression <em>“to laity of the Innovation,”</em> the word Innovation and its meaning is mistaken and misleading, because Ecumenism is not simply an Innovation, nor a newly-appeared uncondemned heresy, <u>but all the condemned heresies together.</u>", "341": "On p. 12 (a2) <em>“The views of Metropolitan Chrysostomos of Etna, which were expressed before or after the Union, should not raise so much concern, for the following reasons: </em>", "342": "<em><strong>• those expressed before the Union, refer to the need to preserve the Principles of Ethos and Moderation, which he received from the late-lamented Metropolitan Cyprian and not to Ecclesiological Positions;”</strong></em>", "343": "(It is a lie that Chrysostomos of Etna referred to Principles of Ethos. He spoke of PRINCIPLES, MODERATION AND SPIRIT!... he said word for word:", "344": "<em>“be assured that none of our principles, none of our moderation and none of the spirit that our ever-memorable and most reverend Metropolitan Cyprian bequeathed to us has been set aside…”</em>", "347": "FOR ALL THESE REASONS THE GREATER ROMANIAN SYNOD UNDER THE LEADERSHIP OF METROPOLITAN EULOGIOS ANATHEMATIZES THE CHURCH OF THE G.O.C. OF GREECE, AFTER THE ROMANIAN SYNOD HAD BROKEN COMMUNION WITH THE SYNOD OF ARCHBISHOP KALLINIKOS UNDER THE LATE-LAMENTED METROPOLITAN DEMOSTHENES AND ACCUSED TWO BISHOPS OF IT AS HERETICS, WHILE THE CHURCH OF THE G.O.C. OF GREECE NEVER BROKE COMMUNION WITH THEM", "348": "THE ANATHEMAS OF THE ROMANIAN SYNOD AGAINST THE CHURCH OF THE G.O.C. OF GREECE ARE AS FOLLOWS:", "349": "The Romanian sister Orthodox Church literally anathematizes:", "351": "<em><strong>IN CONCLUSION, WE SAY TO ALL THOSE WHO:</strong></em>", "352": "<em><strong>…</strong><br>- Regard heretics as part, or as being able to be part, of the Church of Christ,<br><br><strong>- Consider that not <u>every orthodox synod could judge, condemn and anathematize heretics without conditions.</u></strong></em>", "353": "<em><strong>- Consider that the Church of Christ is not spotless and blameless, teaching that heretics are or can be members of the Church of Christ, thereby attacking the holiness of the Church.</strong></em>", "354": "<em><strong>- Consider the Ecumenist, neo-Calvinist and Sergianist “churches” to be Orthodox and possessing Holy Grace.</strong></em>", "355": "<em><strong>…</strong></em><br/>\n<em><strong>- <u>Administer to heretics and schismatics the Mystery of the Divine Eucharist as if it were useful for their salvation.</u></strong></em>", "356": "<em><strong><u>- Have drawn up and support the non-Orthodox teaching called the “theory of the sick member,” which is expressed chiefly through the writing of the text of the “Ecclesiological Positions.”</u></strong></em>", "357": "<em><br/><strong>- <u>The heresy known as the “Theory of the diseased member,”</u> as well as <u>the work entitled “Ecclesiological Positions,”</u> whose authors and unrepentant supporters essentially claim that the Ecumenist heretics are members of the One, Holy, Sovereign and Apostolic Church until a Great Synod is proclaimed and decides it.</strong> <u><strong>Thus all forms of this heresy are also condemned, including the expression of the idea that the Ecumenist heretics (or heretics in general) can be in the One, Holy, Sovereign and Apostolic Church until a Great Synod is convened to pronounce their condemnation</strong>.</u></em>", "358": "<em><br/><strong><u>ANATHEMA!<br/></u></strong></em><br/>\n<em><strong>SECRETARIAT OF THE HOLY SYNOD</strong></em>", "359": "Why <u>must he be anathematized</u>", "360": "Why must <em><strong>Cyprianism or Cyprianitism,</strong></em> the <strong>text <em>Ecclesiological Positions</em> and those who wrote it</strong> be anathematized synodically?", "361": "Precisely because they have been anathematized by all jurisdictions throughout the world and <strong>all the other Synods of the Old Calendarists in Greece, and also by individual bishops (in Greece) and in the world, and the Holy Monastery of Esphigmenou</strong> and <strong>many of the Fathers in the ascetic Cells of Mount Athos</strong> have broken communion with it.", "362": "1. Because those who came from the Cyprianites into the synod church of the G.O.C. of Greece <u>and a multitude of G.O.C. priests,</u> influenced by Crypto-Ecumenism <u>or, according to others, open</u> Ecumenism, <u>commune all the New Calendarists,</u> in Attica-Athens, Piraeus, Thessaloniki, Patras, Agrinio and Northern and Western Greece more generally,", "363": "2. because the above and those of the church of the G.O.C. who are swept along (like the Bishop of Attica, Mr. Maniotis Chrysostomos) do not anathematize the Newly-appeared great heresies such as, e.g., the heresy of Kolymbari, preached for the first time on such a scale worldwide and institutionally, where Ecumenism was made into a church,", "364": "3. because they refuse the supreme duty and mission of the Orthodox Synod, to anathematize the preached heresies, refusing to condemn the Kolymbarists,", "365": "4. and because the false doctrine is preached that supposedly some time in the future, by some synod, somewhere, which will be pan-orthodox, the matters of the heresy of Ecumenism will be resolved, since the Ecumenists are supposedly still unjudged, while the heresy of Ecumenism reaps souls leading them to perdition and eternal condemnation", "366": "5. the faithful New Calendarists and Ecumenists mix with one another at various ecclesiastical events, e.g., chanting together and celebrating together on Palm Sunday in Attica, in the province of the Bishop of Attica, Mr. Maniotis Chrysostomos, or at the meetings of the epitaphioi every Great Friday in Attica,", "367": "6. the Cyprianites and many of the G.O.C. allow the New Calendarist faithful to commune, the New Calendarist Ecumenists, both at the New and at the Old,", "368": "7. the Faithful celebrate, because of the general laxity and the general indifference of the synod of the G.O.C. toward the Orthodox Faith in many regions, Christmas both with the New and with the Old,", "369": "8. and because the blasphemous theory <em>of sick members of the Ecumenists,</em> (proclaimed worldwide by the Cyprianites), was never anathematized, <u>a multitude of hearths of Cyprianite ideology and of heretical teaching of this abominable heresy are maintained, in Greece and abroad,</u> that the mysteries of the New Calendarists-Ecumenists, <u>who are supposedly <em>“unjudged,”</em></u> are still valid, since supposedly no <em>“pan-orthodox synod”</em> has condemned Ecumenism.", "370": "9. The anathema against Ecumenism of Saint Philaret in 1983 in Montreal, Canada, is not enough for them, nor the Anathema against Ecumenism of 1998 of the Synod under our Blessed Archbishop Chrysostomos II, nor the Anathema against Ecumenism of the Romanian Synod of 2013 under Metropolitan Vlasios and of other orthodox synods less known in Greece and throughout the world.", "371": "See the relevant links below, besides the anathemas against the church of the G.O.C. of Greece by the bishops of Slatioara in communion with the church of the G.O.C. of Romania -(the church of the G.O.C. never cut them off to this day)-, under Metropolitan Demosthenes and under Eulogios, mentioned above, and the relevant links!", "381": "A multitude of Genuine Orthodox throughout the world, on Mount Athos and in Greece have condemned the Cyprianite heresy and have anathematized the text <em>Ecclesiological Positions</em> and those who wrote it!", "385": "Fr. Nicholas Dimaras Dr. Jur. N. Dimaras, <a href=\"mailto:dikaio@otenet.gr\"><u>&lt;dikaio@otenet.gr&gt;</u></a>", "389": "Dr. NIKOLAOS DIMARAS <a href=\"mailto:dikaio@otenet.gr\"><u>&lt;dikaio@otenet.gr&gt;</u></a>", "390": "Why must <em><strong>Cyprianism or Cyprianitism,</strong></em> the <strong>text <em>Ecclesiological Positions</em></strong> and <strong><em>those who wrote it</em></strong> be anathematized?", "391": "Precisely because they have broken communion or even <strong>anathematized,</strong> or do not wish any communication with the church of the G.O.C. of Greece, all the Genuine Orthodox jurisdictions throughout the world and <strong>almost all the Synods of the Old Calendarists in Greece, and also individual bishops, the Holy Monastery of Esphigmenou</strong> and <strong>a multitude of Fathers in the various Cells of Mount Athos, as we analyzed for the following reasons and the further explanations on the basis of the teaching of the Ecumenical Synods and the Holy Fathers:</strong>", "392": "<em><strong>1. Because those coming from the Cyprianites into the Synod church of the G.O.C. of Greece <u>and a multitude of our G.O.C. priests,</u> influenced by Crypto-Ecumenism (or, according to many, open Ecumenism), commune all the New Calendarists, in Athens, Piraeus, Thessaloniki, Patras and Western Greece more generally, </strong></em>", "393": "<em><strong>2. because they do not anathematize the Newly-appeared heresies such as, e.g., that of Kolymbari, </strong></em>", "394": "<em><strong>3. because they refuse the supreme duty and mission of the Orthodox Synod, to anathematize the preached heresies, </strong></em>", "395": "<em><strong>4. and because the false doctrine is preached that supposedly some time in the future, by some synod, which will be pan-orthodox, the matters of the heresy of Ecumenism, preached for a hundred years, will be resolved, while in the meantime the heresy of Ecumenism reaps souls, </strong></em>", "396": "5. whereas the Ecumenical Synod makes a <u>diagnosis of the already occurred rotting</u> and <u>of the self-severance of the heretics from the Church,</u> whom it also anathematizes (<u>Synodikon of Orthodoxy,</u> <em>Triodion,</em> p. 146, 2nd ed. of the Apostoliki Diakonia of the Church of Greece, Athens, 1993. See also Ioannis Romanides, <em>Dogmatics,</em> vol. 2): <em>“<u>to those, then, who irretrievably are held by this error,</u> and have their ears stopped against every divine word and spiritual teaching, <u>as those already rotten</u> and <u>who have cut themselves off from the common body of the Church,</u> anathema.”</em>", "397": "The Holy Sixth and Seventh Ecumenical Synods anathematize and condemn all the heretics, declaring: <em>“To all the heretics, anathema. To all who lay claim to the things of the heretics, anathema; this is the faith of the Christians”!</em> And we, as children of obedience, simply repeat what the God-bearing Fathers first proclaimed, when, in the holy Seventh Ecumenical Synod, <strong><u>they proclaim the anathema also for all that will be done after the holy Seventh Ecumenical Synod and is contrary to the formulation and the teaching of the Ecumenical Synods and of the Holy and God-bearing Fathers.</u></strong>", "398": "In the work of <strong>Photios the Great</strong> <em>“Syntagma of the Canons</em><a class=\"footnote-ref\" href=\"#fn2\" id=\"fnref2\" role=\"doc-noteref\"><sup>2</sup></a> the following are also stated: <em><strong>“All things innovated and done contrary to the ecclesiastical tradition and the teaching and formulation of the holy and blessed Fathers, or to be done hereafter, anathema”</strong></em><a class=\"footnote-ref\" href=\"#fn3\" id=\"fnref3\" role=\"doc-noteref\"><sup>3</sup></a><em><strong>.</strong></em> These Fathers, deliberating synodically, anathematize, among other things, also every future innovation.", "399": "Those who say that, in order for the anathematization of the <strong>Apostle Paul</strong> to have force, supposedly “<em>the Synod must take it up, which will judge and condemn the heretical Bishop,”</em> are mistaken<em>.</em> If this is so, then even more the future anathematization of these Fathers does not hold, and indeed for innovations that concern the teaching of the holy Fathers and the Ecclesiastical Tradition. Then in that case, in the <strong>Synodikon of the Seventh Ecumenical</strong> this anathematization, according to them, would have to be a mistake!", "400": "And <strong>the Great apostle Paul</strong> has this authority to anathematize the heretics of all ages, and the Fathers of the Seventh Ecumenical Synod have the authority to anathematize the future heretics, and even individual bishops, priests and Fathers.", "401": "<strong>Saint Theodore the Studite</strong> in this regard states the following: <em><strong>“but if there be anyone else of the same name as these, yet a heretic according to their heresy or another, whether bishop, or ascetic, or anyone whatever, let him be anathema. And <u>if anyone does not anathematize in due time, as necessary, every heretic, let him be of their party</u>”</strong></em><a class=\"footnote-ref\" href=\"#fn4\" id=\"fnref4\" role=\"doc-noteref\"><sup>4</sup></a><em><strong>.</strong></em> And in another letter, too, the saint states: <em><strong>“Since everyone who is orthodox in all things anathematizes every heretic, in potentiality if not in word”</strong></em><a class=\"footnote-ref\" href=\"#fn5\" id=\"fnref5\" role=\"doc-noteref\"><sup>5</sup></a><em><strong>.</strong></em> It should be noted that both these passages of <strong>Saint Theodore the Studite</strong> are from letters that he sent during the period of the Moechian heresy.", "402": "<em><strong>“And if very few remain in piety and Orthodoxy, these are the Church, and the authority and the protection of the ecclesiastical institutions lies with them, even if they must suffer ill for the sake of piety”</strong></em>", "403": "<em>(“<strong>but if the very least</strong> <strong>remain in piety and orthodoxy,</strong> then <strong>they are the Church and upon them rests the validity and the protection of the ecclesiastical institutions,</strong> even if they must suffer greatly for the sake of piety”</em>", "404": "Saint Nikephoros the monk. P.G. 99, 1049)", "405": "On Fri 28 Feb 2025 at 6:30 a.m., Fr. Nikolaos Dimaras Dr. Jur. N. Dimaras, &lt;<a href=\"mailto:dikaio@otenet.gr\"><u>dikaio@otenet.gr</u></a>&gt; wrote:", "414": "1. It is not enough, patristically (nor logically nor in terms of legislative technique!) to say that with the newly agreed texts the force of previous heretical texts is lifted, <u>which constituted blasphemies and heresies, such as those contained in the text <em>“Ecclesiological Positions.”</em></u> <strong><u>It must expressly and categorically be anathematized and its force lifted officially and in writing, with the lifting of its force and its anathematization being published compulsorily.</u></strong> This must be done, so that no one can ever invoke it, as several still invoke it today and base their positions on it, forming separate communities. And many others will invoke it in the future. <strong><u>Today history is being written! An example is being left to be avoided!</u></strong>", "415": "<u>2. <strong>The authors of this text must also be anathematized. This we received from our Fathers and see it in the Minutes of the Ecumenical Synods. </strong></u>", "416": "Why must this be done?", "417": "So that both the living and those after us may be made an example of, and so that <strong>this false doctrine may not revive again,</strong> since <strong>the daring will tremble at the anathematization,</strong> that is, those who dare to do something of the kind, since the first authors were anathematized. And <strong>the Orthodox will be able to invoke this anathema against anyone who dares to restore it to force or to apply it as never abolished!</strong> Since it was never abolished, it has not ceased to be in force and the authors of such an abominable and heretical text were not anathematized!", "418": "3. <strong>The accompanying text,</strong> which needs interpretation, despite the fact that it was drawn up to interpret the matters of the Unification Text and to normalize the entry of the Cyprianites into the church of the G.O.C. of Greece, <strong>without condemning and anathematizing the proclamation of the Cyprianites</strong> <em><strong>“ecclesiological positions,”</strong></em> which <strong>constituted the institutional and synodal faith of the so-called Resisters, excludes the possibility of anathematization and expression of synodal disapproval with the relevant anathema of any heresy</strong> and downgrades, or <strong>rather abolishes the role of the Orthodox Local Synods,</strong> since it does not give them the possibility to anathematize every heresy, <u>shifting to the indefinite future, to a supposedly some day and somewhere to be convened <em>“pan-orthodox”</em> synod this mission…</u> <strong>For this reason there was no condemnation at all,</strong> for example, <strong>of the ecclesiologically proclaimed and made-into-a-church Ecumenist heresy of Kolymbari.</strong> Thus <strong><u>there is applied in practice the proclaimed heresy of Cyprianism,</u></strong> which <u>is based on the text <em>“Ecclesiological Positions,”</em> revived each time, whose force has never been abolished and lifted and which has never been anathematized in writing, expressly and publicly, together with its authors!</u>", "419": "In this text, which still constitutes the belief of the Cyprianites and of a multitude of bishops, priests, monks and laity throughout Greece, is the cause why almost all the Cyprianites, chiefly priests, are so lax and do not fear to administer the Immaculate Mysteries to the Ecumenists-New Calendarists. <strong>All the mysteries,</strong> <u>not only Holy Communion!</u> They perform mixed marriages, of New Calendarists and Old Calendarists, they administer the unction to everyone, they baptize with New Calendarist godparents and many other things. It is ascertained, then, in practice, how great pastoral and didactic significance the anathematization of such a text would have for the whole Church. There are mentioned <strong>many cases from the Ecumenical Synods in which this happened in the past.</strong>", "420": "5. <strong>The anathema of the Romanians concerns exclusively the church of the G.O.C. of Greece. And it is very strong,</strong> because <u>on the one hand it is the most populous synod in number of faithful in the sphere of the struggling Orthodox,</u> but chiefly, <strong>because it was in communion with the church of the G.O.C. and co-signed the Unification Text of 2014 and the church of the G.O.C. has never officially broken communion with them.</strong> <u>They broke communion <strong>and accuse two bishops plus one now, three,</strong> as heretics</u>. <strong>Therefore the church of the G.O.C. recognized them and still recognizes them as brethren and most canonical bishops and their synod as a canonical synod, and in communion with the church of the G.O.C. of Greece. From the standpoint of Canon and Ecclesiastical Law their anathematization is most valid and the breaking of their communion with the church of the G.O.C. most canonical.</strong>", "421": "6. <u>Consequently, the bishops accused as heretics by the greater Romanian Synod cannot constitute any court from the standpoint of Canon and Ecclesiastical Law,</u> <strong>being themselves liable to trial and accused of heresy, the whole Synod, but especially the three bishops mentioned.</strong>", "422": "7. <strong>The Unification Text calls the New Calendarists-Ecumenists false bishops and fallen from the faith. What does this mean? That they are unholy,</strong> as was also rightly stressed, before many brethren, at Saint Mark of Patras. The text of the Ecclesiological positions of the Cyprianites is therefore fully applied in this case, in which the Bishop of Attica, Mr. Maniotis, is covered by the synod of the church of the G.O.C., while <u>he fraternizes with them, wallows spiritually with them, recognizes them by his successive public and manifest heretical moves and actions!</u> <strong>Precisely this, then, happens because Cyprianism has come to dominate in its whole extent in the synod of the church of the G.O.C. of Greece, an association recognized by law.</strong>", "423": "<strong>The effect of this text is enormous and destructive for the Orthodox confession.</strong> <u>It has unnerved the Orthodox</u> and has dismantled every Orthodox resistance, having brought about general paralysis in the body of the Orthodox, who fell asleep, lulled by the dogmatic minimalism of the Cyprianites, <strong>since this heresy, unfortunately, now runs in the veins of the whole Orthodox church of the G.O.C. of Greece of the Old Calendar and became faith and practice in very many of its priests and hierarchs and not only of the former Cyprianites, in Greece but also worldwide!</strong>", "425": "<em><strong>Fr. Nicholas Dimaras</strong></em>", "426": "The Bishop of Indonesia, Mr. Daniel Biantoro, bishop of the church of the G.O.C. of Greece, Great Ecumenist, and his priests praying together with the Protestants and preaching inside Protestant counter-synagogues. Not even the New Calendarists do these things!", "428": "<em><strong>“Saint Metropolitan Philaret</strong> was the embodiment of the spirit of preserving what has been handed down with fidelity and steadfastness and of repelling the spirit of relativization of the Ecumenists, who embody the lukewarmness, the impermissible syncretistic mixture, for which the Angel of the Church in Laodicea is rebuked, with the threat that God will spue him out, because he ought to be hot or cold and not lukewarm<strong>. Ecumenism and relativism, like secularization, constitute a disgusting mixture of lukewarmness, which constitutes the spirit of “Apostasy,” which aims to deceive even the elect!</strong>”</em>", "429": "<strong>Bishop Clement, <em>Saint Philaret,</em></strong> <em>Fyli, Attica 2015, p. 130.</em>", "430": "Saint Philaret Metropolitan of New York and Venerable Andrew of New Diveyevo", "432": "This lukewarmness and the spirit of relativization of all things of the Ecumenists, Ecumenism and Relativism, which constitutes the spirit of Apostasy, which aims to deceive even the elect, is represented, as has been resoundingly demonstrated by its choices and its decisions, by the church of the G.O.C. of Greece!", "433": "Footnotes", "434": "See <strong>Saint Theodore the Studite,</strong> PG vol. 99, col. 1101-1108, <strong>Epistle 53, To Stephen the reader and those with him</strong>, E.L.I.<a class=\"footnote-back\" href=\"#fnref1\" role=\"doc-backlink\">↩︎</a>", "435": "Title 1 Chap. 2<a class=\"footnote-back\" href=\"#fnref2\" role=\"doc-backlink\">↩︎</a>", "436": "EPE 10, 30.<a class=\"footnote-back\" href=\"#fnref3\" role=\"doc-backlink\">↩︎</a>"};
